  recipeId: diagnostics
  concept: 'Authored objective: Repair all three timing faults and retest.

    Authored
    requirement: Diagnose and isolate V06, C1 and the Q1 bridge in sequence. Capture
    a fresh powered result after each repair.

    General teaching principle: Troubleshooting
    compares fresh evidence with a known reference, isolates likely causes, repairs
    the supported issue and retests.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: Debugging a chain is easier when each link is tested before replacing
    the next.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An absent output is a symptom, not definitive proof that one specific
    component has failed.
